    "response": "Unlike general-purpose language models that are trained on diverse multilingual data to understand multiple languages broadly, local language models concentrate on a single or closely related group of dialects and idioms. They provide more nuanced understanding and generation for specific linguistic contexts by learning from regionally prevalent text samples."
